The MIT License above covers the joshw-browser source code only. joshw-browser
relies on, downloads, builds or bundles the open-source projects below. Each
one remains under its own license and copyright, held by its authors. Thank
you to all of them; this program would not exist without their work.

Where a binary is bundled (assets/libraries/), its source and version are
recorded in the SOURCE.txt file next to it, and any license files shipped with
it are kept alongside.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Playback engines and decoders
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Game Music Emu (libgme)
  NSF, SPC, GBS, HES, KSS, AY, SAP, GYM and VGM playback.
  https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu
  License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
  Windows: libgme.dll (cross-compiled, bundled). Linux: system package.

Audio Overload SDK (AOSDK), via the DeaDBeeF psf plugin
  PSF and PSF2 playback (libaosdk.so / aosdk.dll, built from
  plugins/psf/aosdk of DeaDBeeF, plus tools/windows_decoders/aosdk_wrapper.c).
  https://github.com/DeaDBeeF-Player/deadbeef/tree/master/plugins/psf
  Copyright (c) 2007 R. Belmont and Richard Bannister (AOSDK);
  Copyright (c) 2009-2014 Oleksiy Yakovenko (DeaDBeeF plugin)
  License: AOSDK engine BSD-3-Clause; P.E.Op.S. SPU/SPU2 sound cores and the
  DeaDBeeF plugin GPL-2.0-or-later. The built libraries are distributed under
  GPL-2.0-or-later.

lazyusf2
  N64 USF playback (usfdec, built from tools/windows_decoders).
  https://github.com/derselbst/lazyusf2
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later (derived from mupen64plus)

lazyusf
  N64 USF playback on Linux (built on your machine by Install Dependencies;
  not bundled).
  https://github.com/derselbst/lazyusf
  License: derived from Project64, which is freeware for personal,
  non-commercial use only. See the source files for the full terms.

psflib
  PSF container loading for the USF and 2SF decoders.
  https://github.com/kode54/psflib
  Copyright (c) 2012-2015 Christopher Snowhill
  License: MIT

playgsf
  GBA GSF playback (Linux playgsf, and gsfdec built from tools/windows_decoders).
  https://github.com/yshui/playgsf
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later (based on VisualBoyAdvance); includes libresample
  (LGPL-2.1)

vio2sf / 2sftowav
  Nintendo DS 2SF playback (Linux 2sfPlay, and 2sfdec built from
  tools/windows_decoders).
  https://github.com/yshui/2sftowav
  License: GPL-2.0 (DeSmuME-derived core)

vgmstream
  Streamed audio formats (BRSTM, DSP, WEM, HCA, ...).
  https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream
  License: ISC-style permissive license (see COPYING), with bundled codec
  libraries under their own licenses.
  Windows: vgmstream-cli.exe (official build, bundled). Linux: vgmstream123.

sidplayfp / libsidplayfp
  Commodore 64 SID playback.
  https://github.com/libsidplayfp/sidplayfp
  https://github.com/libsidplayfp/libsidplayfp
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Windows: sidplayfp.exe (official build, bundled). Linux: system package.

VGMPlay
  Arcade VGZ playback.
  https://github.com/vgmrips/vgmplay-legacy
  License: GPL (sound cores from MAME, DOSBox, openMSX, Gens/GS, NSFPlay,
  EMU2149/EMU2413 and others under their own licenses; see VGMPlay/licenses
  in the repository).

NeoBAE (Beatnik Audio Engine / miniBAE)
  MIDI, RMF, XMF and other Beatnik formats (playbae).
  https://github.com/zefie/NeoBAE
  License: NeoBAE modifications LGPL-3.0; original Beatnik miniBAE
  BSD-3-Clause.

mpv
  MP3, OGG, FLAC, tracker modules and other general audio.
  https://mpv.io  /  https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv
  Windows builds: https://github.com/shinchiro/mpv-winbuild-cmake
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later (LGPL-2.1-or-later when built without GPL parts)

HivelyTracker (hvl2wav)
  AHX and HivelyTracker (.ahx, .hvl) playback and export (hvl2wav, built
  from tools/windows_decoders).
  https://github.com/pete-gordon/hivelytracker
  Copyright (c) Peter Gordon (Xeron/IRIS); AHX replayer based on work by
  Dexter/Abyss
  License: BSD-3-Clause

libopenmpt (via FFmpeg in mpv)
  Tracker module playback (MOD, XM, IT, S3M, MPTM, MO3, MED, ...).
  https://lib.openmpt.org
  License: BSD-3-Clause

WildMIDI
  Converting .xmi files to MIDI on Linux (optional).
  https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi
  License: library LGPL-3.0, player GPL-3.0


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tools and libraries used by the decoders
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7-Zip (7za.exe)
  Extracting .7z archives on Windows.
  https://github.com/ip7z/7zip  /  https://www.7-zip.org
  Copyright (c) 1999-2026 Igor Pavlov
  License: GNU LGPL, with some code under BSD-3-Clause and BSD-2-Clause
  (see assets/libraries/windows/7zip/License.txt)

SDL2, SDL3 and SDL3_ttf
  Audio output for the Linux decoders and NeoBAE.
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_ttf
  License: zlib

zlib
  Decompression inside several decoders.
  https://zlib.net
  License: zlib

libao
  Audio output for playgsf on Linux.
  https://xiph.org/ao/
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python libraries
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Python and Tkinter (Tcl/Tk)
  https://www.python.org  /  https://www.tcl.tk
  License: PSF License; Tcl/Tk BSD-style license

ttkbootstrap
  Themed user interface.
  https://github.com/israel-dryer/ttkbootstrap
  License: MIT

Pillow
  Images, icons and box art.
  https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow
  License: MIT-CMU (HPND)

python-sounddevice (with PortAudio)
  Audio output for the in-process players.
  https://github.com/spatialaudio/python-sounddevice
  https://www.portaudio.com
  License: MIT

Mido
  MIDI file handling.
  https://github.com/mido/mido
  License: MIT

NumPy
  Fast volume and fade processing.
  https://github.com/numpy/numpy
  License: BSD-3-Clause

python-soundfile (with libsndfile)
  FLAC export.
  https://github.com/bastibe/python-soundfile
  https://github.com/libsndfile/libsndfile
  License: BSD-3-Clause; libsndfile LGPL-2.1-or-later

pystray
  System tray icon.
  https://github.com/moses-palmer/pystray
  License: LGPL-3.0

Jeepney
  Media keys and desktop media controls (MPRIS over D-Bus) on Linux.
  https://gitlab.com/takluyver/jeepney
  License: MIT

pycaw and comtypes
  Per-player volume control on Windows.
  https://github.com/AndreMiras/pycaw
  https://github.com/enthought/comtypes
  License: MIT

PyInstaller
  Building the single-file executables.
  https://github.com/pyinstaller/pyinstaller
  License: GPL-2.0 with a bootloader exception (applications built with it
  may use any license).


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data and content (downloaded at run time, not bundled)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

joshw.info
  The video game music archives this program browses. All music remains
  the property of its respective copyright holders.
  https://joshw.info

VGMusic
  MIDI archive (VGMusic Siterip domain).
  https://www.vgmusic.com

The Mod Archive
  Tracker modules (Chiptune domain). All modules remain the property of
  their respective authors.
  https://modarchive.org

libretro-thumbnails
  Box art shown in the Game Info panel and Now Playing window. All images
  remain the property of their respective copyright holders.
  https://github.com/libretro-thumbnails/libretro-thumbnails
  https://thumbnails.libretro.com

FluidR3 GM SoundFont
  Default MIDI soundfont.
  https://github.com/pianobooster/fluid-soundfont
  Copyright (c) Frank Wen
  License: MIT

Commodore 64 KERNAL and BASIC ROMs
  Needed by sidplayfp; downloaded from zimmers.net on request. Copyright
  Commodore and its successors.
  https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/c64/
